Request Result Path that no rule matches, for example <code>/api/nothing/here</code> HTTP 404, JSON <code>{"exc_type": "DoesNotExistError"}</code> (v2: <code>{"errors": [{"type": "DoesNotExistError"}]}</code>) Path matches, HTTP method does not, for example <code>DELETE /api/v2/doctype/ToDo/meta</code> HTTP 405, Werkzeug HTML page, not JSON <code>GET /api/v2/method/logout</code> The <code>POST</code> rule does not match, so <code>/method/&lt;method&gt;</code> resolves <code>logout</code> as a dotted path. HTTP 417 <code>AppNotInstalledError</code> "App logout is not installed" <pre><code>curl -s -X DELETE "$S/api/v2/doctype/ToDo/meta" -b cookies.txt -w '\n%{http_code}\n'
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang=en&gt;
&lt;title&gt;405 Method Not Allowed&lt;/title&gt;
...
405
</code></pre>

v1 (<code>/api/...</code>, <code>/api/v1/...</code>) v2 (<code>/api/v2/...</code>) Method result <code>message</code> <code>data</code> Resource result <code>data</code> <code>data</code> Messages <code>_server_messages</code> (JSON string) <code>messages</code> (list) Error <code>exc_type</code>, <code>exception</code>, <code>exc</code>, <code>_server_messages</code> <code>errors</code>: list with one object Error message text in <code>_server_messages</code> in <code>errors[0].message</code> <p>v1 error keys (<code>report_error()</code> in <code>frappe/utils/response.py</code>):</p> Key Content When <code>exc_type</code> Class name of the exception always <code>exception</code> Last line of the traceback, for example <code>frappe.exceptions.PermissionError: Not permitted</code> tracebacks allowed <code>exc</code> JSON string of a list with the full traceback tracebacks allowed <code>_server_messages</code> The <code>throw</code> message when the code called <code>frappe.throw</code> or <code>msgprint</code> <p>v2 error object keys: <code>type</code>, <code>exception</code> (full traceback, when allowed), and the keys of the linked <code>throw</code> message (<code>message</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>indicator</code>, <code>as_table</code>).</p> <p>Tracebacks are allowed (<code>is_traceback_allowed()</code>) on the development server (<code>bench start</code> sets <code>DEV_SERVER</code>), or when System Settings <code>allow_error_traceback</code> is on (default <code>1</code>) and the user is a System User. They are never sent for HTTP 404, unless site config <code>logging</code> is set. A CSRF error turns them off.</p> <p>The same Guest call, on a production-like server (no <code>DEV_SERVER</code>):</p> <pre><code>{"exc_type": "PermissionError",
 "_server_messages": "[\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"&lt;p&gt;You are not permitted to access this resource. Login to access&lt;/p&gt;...\\\", ...}\"]"}
</code></pre> <p>Warning</p> <p>An error raised without <code>frappe.throw</code> has no message. For example, <code>frappe.FrappeTypeError</code> from type validation. Without tracebacks, a v2 client gets only <code>{"errors": [{"type": "FrappeTypeError"}]}</code>, and a v1 client gets only <code>exc_type</code>.</p>

Hook Called with Applies to <code>has_permission</code> <code>doc, ptype, user, debug</code> One document: v1 and v2 read, create, update, delete and document methods. A falsy return denies. It cannot grant. <code>permission_query_conditions</code> <code>user, doctype=</code> Lists: v1 <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;</code> (<code>frappe.get_list</code>), v2 <code>/api/v2/document/&lt;doctype&gt;</code> (<code>frappe.qb.get_query</code>). Returns an SQL condition string. <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
has_permission = {"ToDo": "sample_app.permissions.todo_has_permission"}
permission_query_conditions = {"ToDo": "sample_app.permissions.todo_query"}
</code></pre> <pre><code># sample_app/permissions.py
def todo_has_permission(doc, ptype, user, debug=False):
    return doc.description != "secret"


def todo_query(user, doctype=None):
    return "`tabToDo`.`description` != 'secret'"
</code></pre> <p>Results for <code>user1@example.com</code>, who owns one ToDo "secret" and one ToDo "Sample visible":</p> Request Result <code>POST /api/v2/document/ToDo</code> with <code>{"description": "secret"}</code> HTTP 403. <code>has_permission</code> was called with <code>ptype="create"</code>. <code>GET /api/v2/document/ToDo/&lt;secret name&gt;</code> HTTP 403. Called with <code>ptype="read"</code>. <code>GET /api/resource/ToDo/&lt;secret name&gt;</code> HTTP 403 <code>GET /api/v2/document/ToDo?fields=["description"]</code> <code>{"has_next_page": false, "data": [{"description": "Sample visible"}]}</code> <code>GET /api/resource/ToDo?fields=["description"]</code> <code>{"data": [{"description": "Sample visible"}]}</code> <p><code>has_permission</code> is not called for list rows. Use both hooks so that a list and a single read give the same answer. Frappe has no <code>write_permission_query_conditions</code> hook. See Permissions.</p> <p>For your own DocType, a static <code>get_list(query)</code> on the controller can also change the v2 list query. See REST API.</p>

Method Returns <code>doc.get_doc_before_save()</code> The stored copy that was loaded at the start of <code>save</code>. <code>None</code> for a new document. <code>doc.has_value_changed(fieldname)</code> <code>True</code> if the field differs from the stored copy. Always <code>True</code> for a new document. <code>doc.get_value_before_save(fieldname)</code> The stored value, or <code>None</code> for a new document. <p>These methods work in every lifecycle method of a save, including <code>on_update</code> and <code>on_change</code>. Child rows have their own <code>get_doc_before_save()</code>.</p> <pre><code>class SampleOrder(Document):
    def on_update(self):
        if self.has_value_changed("status"):
            old = self.get_value_before_save("status")
            self.add_comment("Info", f"Status changed from {old} to {self.status}")
</code></pre>

Function Description <code>frappe.msgprint(message, title)</code> Show a message dialog. <code>frappe.msgprint({message, title, indicator, primary_action, wide})</code> The same, with options. <code>indicator</code> is a color, for example <code>"red"</code>. <code>frappe.throw(message)</code> Show a red message and throw an <code>Error</code>. Stops the code that called it, for example a <code>validate</code> handler. <code>frappe.show_alert({message, indicator}, seconds)</code> Show a toast. Default 7 seconds. <code>frappe.toast</code> is the same function. <code>frappe.confirm(message, on_yes, on_no)</code> Ask Yes or No. Returns the dialog. <code>frappe.warn(title, message, on_proceed, primary_label)</code> A confirm dialog with a red primary button, for destructive actions. <code>frappe.prompt(fields, callback, title, primary_label)</code> Ask for values. <code>fields</code> is a label string, one field or a list of fields. <code>frappe.show_progress(title, count, total, description)</code> Show a progress bar dialog. <code>frappe.hide_progress()</code> closes it. <pre><code>frappe.confirm(__("Mark all open orders as completed?"), () =&gt; {
    frappe.xcall("sample_app.api.complete_open_orders").then(() =&gt;
        frappe.show_alert({ message: __("Done"), indicator: "green" })
    );
});

frappe.prompt(
    { label: __("Customer"), fieldname: "customer_name", fieldtype: "Data", reqd: 1 },
    (values) =&gt; frappe.new_doc("Sample Order", values),
    __("New Order")
);
</code></pre>

Function Description <code>frappe.set_route(...parts)</code> Go to a desk route. Returns a promise. <code>frappe.get_route()</code> The current route as a list, for example <code>["Form", "Sample Order", "SO-00001"]</code>. <code>frappe.get_route_str()</code> The current route as a string. <code>frappe.route_options</code> Values for the next view. A list view uses them as filters. A new form uses them as field values. <code>frappe.get_prev_route()</code> The previous route. <pre><code>frappe.set_route("List", "Sample Order");
frappe.set_route("Form", "Sample Order", "SO-00001");
frappe.set_route("sample-order/new");

frappe.route_options = { status: "Open" };
frappe.set_route("List", "Sample Order"); // the list opens with status = Open
</code></pre> <p><code>frappe.set_route</code> accepts separate parts, a list or one string with slashes. <code>List</code>, <code>Form</code>, <code>Tree</code> and <code>Report</code> are converted to URL routes, for example <code>/desk/sample-order/SO-00001</code>. The desk can add the sidebar name to the URL. Do not build desk URLs by hand. Use <code>frappe.utils.get_form_link(doctype, name)</code> for a link.</p>

Queue Default timeout <code>short</code> 300 seconds <code>default</code> 300 seconds <code>long</code> 1500 seconds <p>Add a queue in <code>sites/common_site_config.json</code> under <code>workers</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
 "workers": {
  "sample_queue": {"timeout": 900}
 }
}
</code></pre> <p>Then start a worker for it: <code>bench worker --queue sample_queue</code>. In production, run <code>bench setup supervisor</code> or <code>bench setup systemd</code> again so a worker serves the new queue.</p> <p>Queue names in Redis are <code>&lt;bench_id&gt;:&lt;queue&gt;</code>, so two benches can share one Redis.</p> <p><code>frappe.enqueue</code> raises <code>frappe.QueueOverloaded</code> when a queue holds too many jobs. The limit is <code>max_queued_jobs</code> (default 500) plus 50 for each site on the bench.</p>

Key Shape Read in Description <code>before_request</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/app.py</code> All run before each HTTP request is handled. No arguments. <code>after_request</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/app.py</code> All run after each request. Called with <code>response=</code> and <code>request=</code>. <code>streaming_request_paths</code> list of str <code>frappe/app.py</code> Request paths (and sub-paths) whose PUT body Frappe does not parse into <code>form_dict</code>. The route must read <code>request.stream</code>. <code>auth_hooks</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/auth.py</code> All run while Frappe validates the request auth. Use them to set the user from a custom header. No arguments. <code>before_login</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/auth.py</code> Runs before username and password are checked. Called with <code>login_manager=</code>. <code>on_login</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/auth.py</code> Runs after a successful login. Called with <code>login_manager=</code>. <code>on_session_creation</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/auth.py</code> Runs after a new session is made. Called with <code>login_manager=</code>. <code>on_logout</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/auth.py</code> Runs on logout, before the session is deleted. Called with <code>login_manager=</code>. <code>on_social_login</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/utils/oauth.py</code> Runs after a social login, before the user is logged in. Called with <code>user=</code>, <code>provider=</code>, <code>claims=</code>. <code>override_whitelisted_methods</code> dict: dotted path -&gt; dotted path <code>frappe/__init__.py</code> Replaces a whitelisted method for <code>/api/method/&lt;path&gt;</code>. Last wins. <code>require_type_annotated_api_methods</code> bool <code>frappe/utils/typing_validations.py</code> Per app. <code>True</code> makes every whitelisted method of the app require type hints, and Frappe validates arguments against them. <code>use_json_request_body</code> bool <code>frappe/boot.py</code> Per app. <code>True</code> makes <code>frappe.call</code> send a JSON body to this app's methods instead of form data. <code>send_token_via_sms</code> dotted path <code>frappe/twofactor.py</code> Last wins. Sends the 2FA OTP by SMS. Called with <code>otpsecret, token, phone_no</code>. <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
before_request = ["sample_app.utils.request.log_path"]
override_whitelisted_methods = {
    "frappe.desk.doctype.event.event.get_events": "sample_app.api.get_events",
}
</code></pre>

Key Shape Read in Description <code>doc_events</code> dict: DocType (or <code>"*"</code>, or tuple of DocTypes) -&gt; event -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/__init__.py</code>, <code>frappe/model/document.py</code> Runs functions on document events (<code>validate</code>, <code>on_update</code>, <code>on_submit</code>, ...). Called with <code>doc, method</code>. See Controllers. <code>override_doctype_class</code> dict: DocType -&gt; dotted class path <code>frappe/model/document.py</code> Replaces the controller class of a DocType. Last wins. Install and migrate warn when two apps override the same DocType. <code>extend_doctype_class</code> dict: DocType -&gt; list of dotted class paths <code>frappe/model/document.py</code> Adds mixin classes to the controller. All classes combine with the base class (later apps first in the MRO). <code>override_doctype_dashboards</code> dict: DocType -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/model/meta.py</code> Changes the connections dashboard. Called with <code>data=</code>. Must return the new data. <code>naming_series_variables</code> dict: variable -&gt; dotted path <code>frappe/model/naming.py</code> Custom parts in naming series, for example <code>.{branch}.</code> Last wins per variable. <code>ignore_links_on_delete</code> list of DocTypes <code>frappe/model/delete_doc.py</code> Links from these DocTypes do not block delete or cancel. <code>auto_cancel_exempted_doctypes</code> list of DocTypes <code>frappe/desk/form/linked_with.py</code> DocTypes that "cancel all linked documents" does not cancel. <code>workflow_methods</code> list of dict (<code>name</code>, <code>method</code>) <code>frappe/model/workflow.py</code>, <code>frappe/workflow/doctype/workflow/workflow.py</code> Adds tasks to choose in a Workflow transition. <code>export_python_type_annotations</code> bool <code>frappe/core/doctype/doctype/doctype.py</code> Per app. <code>True</code> writes type hints into the controller when a DocType is saved in developer mode. <code>domains</code> dict: domain -&gt; dotted module <code>frappe/__init__.py</code>, <code>frappe/core/doctype/domain/domain.py</code> Domain setup data. The module must have a <code>data</code> attribute. <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
doc_events = {
    "Sample Order": {
        "validate": "sample_app.events.sample_order.validate",
        "on_submit": ["sample_app.events.sample_order.notify"],
    },
    "*": {"on_trash": "sample_app.events.audit.log_delete"},
}
override_doctype_class = {"ToDo": "sample_app.overrides.todo.SampleToDo"}
extend_doctype_class = {"User": ["sample_app.overrides.user.UserMixin"]}
</code></pre>

Key Shape Read in Description <code>has_permission</code> dict: DocType or <code>"*"</code> -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/permissions.py</code> Called with <code>doc, ptype, user, debug</code>. A falsy return denies access. It cannot grant access. <code>permission_query_conditions</code> dict: DocType or <code>"*"</code> -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/model/db_query.py</code>, <code>frappe/database/query.py</code> Called with <code>user, doctype=</code>. Returns an SQL condition string that <code>get_list</code> adds to the query. <code>has_website_permission</code> dict: DocType -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/__init__.py</code>, <code>frappe/website/page_renderers/not_found_page.py</code> Permission check for portal pages of a DocType, when the controller has no <code>has_website_permission</code> method. <code>has_comment_permission</code> dict with <code>doctype</code> and <code>method</code> <code>frappe/templates/includes/comments/comments.py</code> Lets Guest post web comments on one more DocType. <code>method</code> is called with <code>ref_doctype=</code>. <code>ignore_file_permissions</code> bool <code>frappe/core/doctype/file/file.py</code> <code>True</code> from any app turns off File permission checks. Use with care. <code>user_invitation</code> dict <code>frappe/core/doctype/user_invitation/user_invitation.py</code>, <code>frappe/core/api/user_invitation.py</code> Per app. Keys: <code>allowed_roles</code> (role -&gt; roles it can invite), <code>extra_invite_params</code> (list), <code>after_accept</code> (dotted paths). <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
has_permission = {"Sample Order": "sample_app.permissions.sample_order_has_permission"}
permission_query_conditions = {"Sample Order": "sample_app.permissions.sample_order_query"}
</code></pre> <pre><code># sample_app/permissions.py
def sample_order_query(user, doctype=None):
    return f"`tabSample Order`.owner_user = {frappe.db.escape(user)}"
</code></pre>

Key Shape Read in Description <code>app_include_js</code> list of str <code>frappe/www/desk.py</code> JS bundles or paths loaded in desk. Also read from site config. <code>app_include_css</code> list of str <code>frappe/www/desk.py</code> CSS loaded in desk. Also read from site config. <code>app_include_icons</code> list of str <code>frappe/www/desk.py</code> SVG sprite files loaded in desk. <code>doctype_js</code> dict: DocType -&gt; path <code>frappe/desk/form/meta.py</code> Extra form script for a DocType of another app. Path is relative to the app package. <code>doctype_list_js</code> dict: DocType -&gt; path <code>frappe/desk/form/meta.py</code> Extra list view script. <code>doctype_tree_js</code> dict: DocType -&gt; path <code>frappe/desk/form/meta.py</code> Extra tree view script. <code>doctype_calendar_js</code> dict: DocType -&gt; path <code>frappe/desk/form/meta.py</code> Extra calendar view script. <code>doctype_kanban_js</code> dict: DocType -&gt; path <code>frappe/desk/form/meta.py</code> Extra kanban view script. <code>page_js</code> dict: page name -&gt; path <code>frappe/core/doctype/page/page.py</code> Extra script for a desk Page. <code>boot_session</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/boot.py</code> Called with <code>bootinfo</code> while desk boot data is built. <code>extend_bootinfo</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/sessions.py</code> Called with <code>bootinfo=</code> after the boot data is built. <code>calendars</code> list of DocTypes <code>frappe/boot.py</code> DocTypes shown as calendars. <code>treeviews</code> list of DocTypes <code>frappe/boot.py</code> DocTypes that open in tree view. <code>filters_config</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/boot.py</code> Each returns a dict of custom filter operators. <code>standard_queries</code> dict: DocType -&gt; dotted path <code>frappe/desk/search.py</code> Default Link field search query for a DocType. Last wins. <code>awesomebar_search</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/search.py</code>, <code>frappe/boot.py</code> Extra awesomebar results. Called with the search text. Returns a list of items. <code>additional_timeline_content</code> dict: DocType or <code>"*"</code> -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/form/load.py</code> Extra timeline items. Called with <code>doctype, docname</code>. Returns a list. <code>notification_config</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/notifications.py</code> Each returns a dict with <code>for_doctype</code>, <code>for_module</code>, <code>for_other</code>, <code>targets</code> for open counts. <code>notification_skip_email_types</code> list of str <code>frappe/desk/doctype/notification_log/notification_log.py</code> Notification Log types that do not send their own email. <code>notification_self_notify_types</code> list of str <code>frappe/desk/doctype/notification_log/notification_log.py</code> Notification Log types that reach the user who caused them. <code>standard_navbar_items</code> list of dict <code>frappe/utils/install.py</code>, <code>frappe/core/doctype/navbar_settings/navbar_settings.py</code> Items for the user (settings) dropdown in Navbar Settings. <code>standard_help_items</code> list of dict <code>frappe/utils/install.py</code>, <code>frappe/core/doctype/navbar_settings/navbar_settings.py</code> Items for the help dropdown. Keys: <code>item_label</code>, <code>item_type</code>, <code>route</code> or <code>action</code>, <code>is_standard</code>. <code>sounds</code> list of dict (<code>name</code>, <code>src</code>, <code>volume</code>) <code>frappe/www/desk.py</code> Sounds that desk can play. <code>global_search_doctypes</code> dict: domain -&gt; list of dict <code>frappe/desk/doctype/global_search_settings/global_search_settings.py</code> Default DocTypes for global search. Per app. <code>clear_cache</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/cache_manager.py</code> Runs on <code>frappe.clear_cache()</code>. <code>persistent_cache_keys</code> list of str (glob) <code>frappe/cache_manager.py</code> Redis keys that <code>clear_cache</code> keeps. <code>setup_wizard_requires</code> list of str <code>frappe/boot.py</code> Assets the setup wizard loads first. <code>setup_wizard_stages</code> dotted path <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> Per app. Returns the stages and tasks of the setup wizard. <code>setup_wizard_complete</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> Run when the setup wizard completes. Called with the wizard args. <code>setup_wizard_success</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> Run after setup succeeds. Called with the args. <code>setup_wizard_exception</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> Run when setup fails. Called with <code>traceback, args</code>. <code>setup_wizard_url</code> str <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> Last wins. Route of a custom setup wizard. <code>setup_wizard_auto_complete</code> bool <code>frappe/desk/page/setup_wizard/setup_wizard.py</code> <code>True</code> lets Frappe complete a prefilled setup without the wizard. <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
app_include_js = "sample_app.bundle.js"
doctype_js = {"ToDo": "public/js/todo.js"}
standard_queries = {"Sample Item": "sample_app.queries.sample_item_query"}
</code></pre>

Key Shape Read in Description <code>scheduler_events</code> dict: event -&gt; dotted paths, <code>cron</code> -&gt; dict: cron string -&gt; dotted paths <code>frappe/core/doctype/scheduled_job_type/scheduled_job_type.py</code> Makes Scheduled Job Type records on migrate. Events: <code>all</code>, <code>hourly</code>, <code>hourly_long</code>, <code>hourly_maintenance</code>, <code>daily</code>, <code>daily_long</code>, <code>daily_maintenance</code>, <code>weekly</code>, <code>weekly_long</code>, <code>monthly</code>, <code>monthly_long</code>, <code>yearly</code>, <code>annual</code>, <code>cron</code>. <code>before_job</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/utils/background_jobs.py</code> Runs before each background job. Called with <code>method=</code>, <code>kwargs=</code>, <code>transaction_type="job"</code>. <code>after_job</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/utils/background_jobs.py</code> Runs after each job. Called with <code>method=</code>, <code>kwargs=</code>, <code>result=</code>. <code>default_log_clearing_doctypes</code> dict: DocType -&gt; days <code>frappe/core/doctype/log_settings/log_settings.py</code>, <code>frappe/commands/site.py</code> Default retention days added to Log Settings. <code>get_site_info</code> list of dotted paths <code>frappe/utils/__init__.py</code> Called with <code>site_info</code>. A returned dict adds data to site usage info. <pre><code># sample_app/hooks.py
scheduler_events = {
    "daily": ["sample_app.tasks.close_old_orders"],
    "cron": {"0/30 * * * *": ["sample_app.tasks.sync_rates"]},
}
</code></pre> <p>See Scheduler and Background Jobs.</p>

Route HTTP methods Does Permission check <code>/api/method/&lt;dotted.path&gt;</code> any allowed by the method Calls a whitelisted function. Also runs API Server Scripts with that name. <code>@frappe.whitelist</code> rules (guest, HTTP methods) <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;</code> <code>GET</code>, <code>QUERY</code> List records through <code>frappe.client.get_list</code>. <code>get_list</code> permission rules <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;</code> <code>POST</code> Insert a document from the JSON body (or <code>data</code>). <code>create</code> <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code> <code>GET</code> Read one document. <code>expand_links=1</code> adds linked documents. <code>read</code> (<code>frappe.read_doc</code>) <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code> <code>PUT</code> Update fields and save. <code>write</code> <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code> <code>DELETE</code> Delete. Returns HTTP 202 and <code>"ok"</code>. <code>delete</code> <code>/api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code> <code>POST</code>, <code>QUERY</code> Call the whitelisted controller method in <code>run_method</code>. <code>write</code> for <code>POST</code>, <code>read</code> for <code>QUERY</code> <p>List parameters for <code>GET /api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;</code>: <code>fields</code>, <code>filters</code>, <code>or_filters</code>, <code>order_by</code>, <code>group_by</code>, <code>limit_start</code>, <code>limit_page_length</code> (or <code>limit</code>, default 20), <code>as_dict</code>, <code>expand</code>, <code>debug</code>. <code>GET /api/resource/&lt;doctype&gt;/&lt;name&gt;?run_method=&lt;method&gt;</code> also calls a document method (kept for old clients).</p> <pre><code>curl -b cookies.txt "http://frappe.localhost:8000/api/resource/ToDo?fields=%5B%22name%22,%22status%22%5D&amp;limit=2"
</code></pre> <pre><code>{"data": [{"name": "ma6l43o453", "status": "Open"}, {"name": "hq7tpg7mhg", "status": "Open"}]}
</code></pre>

Method or property Description <code>doc</code> The row data. <code>toggle_view(show, callback)</code> Open or close the row form. <code>get_field(fieldname)</code> Return the control of a field in the editable row or the open row form. Throws if neither exists. <code>set_field_property(fieldname, property, value)</code> Set a property on the controls of this row and render them. <code>toggle_reqd(fieldname, reqd)</code>, <code>toggle_display(fieldname, show)</code>, <code>toggle_editable(fieldname, editable)</code> Set <code>reqd</code>, <code>hidden</code> or <code>read_only</code> on the controls of this row. <code>refresh()</code>, <code>refresh_field(fieldname, txt)</code> Render the row or one cell. <code>select(checked)</code> Set <code>doc.__checked</code>. <code>remove()</code> Run <code>before_&lt;table&gt;_remove</code>, remove the row, run <code>&lt;table&gt;_remove</code>. <code>insert(show, below, duplicate)</code> Add a row above or below, or a copy. <code>move()</code> Ask for a row number and move the row. <code>open_prev()</code>, <code>open_next()</code>, <code>has_prev()</code>, <code>has_next()</code> Move between row forms. <pre><code>frappe.ui.form.on("Sample Order", {
    refresh(frm) {
        const grid = frm.get_field("items").grid;
        grid.toggle_enable("rate", false);
        grid.add_custom_button(__("Set Qty to 1"), () =&gt; {
            for (const row of frm.doc.items || []) {
                frappe.model.set_value(row.doctype, row.name, "qty", 1);
            }
        });
    },
});
</code></pre> <p>See Table fields for which calls render and which run events.</p>

Function Description <code>frappe.xcall(method, params, type, opts = {})</code> Promise wrapper of <code>frappe.call</code>. <code>type</code> defaults to <code>"POST"</code>. Resolves with <code>r.message</code>. Rejects with <code>r?.message</code> of the error argument, which is often <code>undefined</code>. <code>opts</code> is spread into the call options. <code>frappe.request.on_error(error_type, handler)</code> Add a global handler for an exception name, for example <code>"DoesNotExistError"</code>. It runs for every call that returns that <code>exc_type</code>. While a handler exists, <code>_server_messages</code> of that call are not shown. <code>frappe.request.app_uses_json(cmd)</code> Return <code>true</code> if the app that owns <code>cmd</code> (first dotted segment) is in <code>frappe.boot.json_request_apps</code>. <code>run_doc_method</code> counts as <code>frappe</code>. <code>frappe.after_ajax(fn)</code> Return a Promise that resolves with <code>fn()</code> after all running requests finish. Runs at once if no request is running. <code>frappe.after_server_call()</code> Return a Promise that resolves when running requests finish, or <code>null</code> if none run. <code>frappe.last_request</code> Data of the last request sent. <code>frappe.last_response</code> Parsed body of the last response. <code>frappe.csrf_token</code> CSRF token sent with each request. <pre><code>const pong = await frappe.xcall("frappe.ping"); // "pong"

frappe.request.on_error("DoesNotExistError", (r) =&gt; {
    console.log("Missing record", r.exc_type);
});
</code></pre> <p>Note</p> <p>On develop, <code>frappe</code> is in <code>frappe.boot.json_request_apps</code>, so calls to <code>frappe.*</code> methods send a JSON body. Apps opt in with <code>use_json_request_body = True</code> in <code>hooks.py</code>. See Whitelisted Methods.</p>

Function Description <code>frappe.provide(namespace)</code> Make nested objects on <code>window</code> for a dotted name. Return the last object. Existing objects are kept. <code>frappe.require(items, callback)</code> Load JS or CSS files. <code>items</code> is a path or a list. Names with <code>.bundle.</code> resolve through <code>frappe.boot.assets_json</code>. Returns a Promise. Calls <code>callback</code> after the Promise resolves. Freezes the page while files load. A file that fails to load still resolves. Each path loads once. <code>frappe.assets.bundled_asset(path, is_rtl = null)</code> Return the built file path of a bundle name, for example <code>"desk.bundle.css"</code>. <pre><code>// sample_app/public/js/sample.js
frappe.provide("sample_app.utils");
sample_app.utils.greet = () =&gt; frappe.show_alert(__("Hello"));

await frappe.require("sample_chart.bundle.js");
</code></pre>

Function Returns Description <code>frappe.msgprint(msg, title, is_minimizable, re_route)</code> <code>frappe.msg_dialog</code> Show a message dialog. <code>msg</code> is a string, a JSON string or an options object (below). A second call before the dialog closes appends the message below a line. Also <code>window.msgprint</code>. <code>frappe.throw(msg)</code> Call <code>frappe.msgprint</code> with a red indicator and the title "Error", then throw <code>Error(msg.message)</code>. <code>msg</code> is a string or an options object. <code>frappe.hide_msgprint(instant)</code> Clear and close the message dialog. <code>instant</code> skips the fade. <code>frappe.update_msgprint(html)</code> Replace the content of the open message dialog. Opens a new one if none is open. <code>frappe.show_alert(message, seconds = 7, actions = {})</code> jQuery element Show a toast. <code>message</code> is a string or <code>{ message, indicator, subtitle, body }</code>. <code>indicator</code> maps to a toast type: <code>green</code> success, <code>red</code> error, <code>orange</code> or <code>yellow</code> warning, <code>blue</code> info. <code>actions</code> maps a <code>data-action</code> value in the message to a click handler. <code>frappe.toast(...)</code> jQuery element Same function as <code>frappe.show_alert</code>. <code>frappe.confirm(message, confirm_action, reject_action, primary_label, secondary_label)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Dialog</code> Show a dialog with "Yes" and "No". <code>reject_action</code> runs when the dialog closes without the primary action. Enter clicks "Yes". <code>frappe.warn(title, message_html, proceed_action, primary_label, is_minimizable, secondary_label)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Dialog</code> Show a warning with a red primary button. <code>secondary_label</code> defaults to "Cancel". <code>frappe.confirm_sensitive_action(callback, message)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Dialog</code> Show a warning titled "Confirm Sensitive Action" with a "Continue" button. <code>frappe.prompt(fields, callback, title, primary_label)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Dialog</code> Ask for values. <code>fields</code> is a field definition, a list of them, or a label string (makes one mandatory Data field named <code>value</code>). <code>callback(values)</code> runs on submit. Default title "Enter Value", default button "Submit". <code>frappe.show_progress(title, count, total = 100, description, hide_on_completion = false)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Dialog</code> Show or update a progress dialog. A call with the same <code>title</code> updates the open dialog. With <code>hide_on_completion</code>, it closes 500 ms after 100 percent. <code>frappe.hide_progress()</code> Close the progress dialog. <code>frappe.messages.waiting(parent, msg)</code> jQuery element Append a centered message box to <code>parent</code>. <code>frappe.messages.get_waiting_message(msg)</code> string HTML of that message box. <p>Options of <code>frappe.msgprint</code> and <code>frappe.throw</code> when <code>msg</code> is an object:</p> Key Description <code>message</code> Text or HTML. A list shows each item with its own <code>msgprint</code> call. In a list from the server, items with <code>raise_exception</code> show first and the others are skipped. <code>title</code> Dialog title. Default "Message". <code>indicator</code> Color of the title indicator. Default <code>blue</code>. <code>as_list</code> Show <code>message</code> (a list) as a bulleted list. <code>as_table</code> Show <code>message</code> (a list of rows) as a table. <code>alert</code>, <code>toast</code> Show as a toast with <code>frappe.show_alert</code> instead of a dialog. <code>clear</code> Clear earlier messages in the open dialog. <code>wide</code> Use the normal dialog width instead of the narrow one. <code>is_minimizable</code> Allow the user to minimize the dialog. <code>re_route</code> Go to the previous route when the dialog closes. <code>primary_action</code> <code>{ label, action }</code>. Or <code>{ label, server_action, args, hide_on_success }</code> to call a whitelisted method. Or <code>{ label, client_action, args }</code> with a dotted path of a global function. <code>secondary_action</code> <code>{ label, action }</code>. Default label "Close". <pre><code>frappe.msgprint({
    title: __("Items"),
    message: [__("Keyboard"), __("Monitor")],
    as_list: 1,
    indicator: "green",
});

frappe.confirm(__("Close this order?"), () =&gt; {
    frappe.show_alert({ message: __("Closed"), indicator: "green" });
});

frappe.prompt(__("Item Name"), ({ value }) =&gt; console.log(value));
</code></pre>

Function Description <code>__(txt, replace, context = null)</code> Return the translation of <code>txt</code> from <code>frappe._messages</code>, or <code>txt</code> if none exists. With <code>context</code>, look up <code>"&lt;txt&gt;:&lt;context&gt;"</code> first. <code>replace</code> is a list (or object) that fills <code>{0}</code>, <code>{1}</code>. A non-string <code>txt</code> is returned as it is. <code>frappe._(txt, replace, context = null)</code> Same function as <code>__</code>. <code>frappe.get_languages()</code> Return <code>[{ label, value }]</code> from <code>frappe.boot.lang_dict</code>, sorted by <code>value</code> (language code). <code>frappe._messages</code> Translation dictionary of the current language. Responses can add to it (<code>__messages</code>). <pre><code>__("Hello {0}", ["World"]); // "Hello World"
__("Confirm", null, "Title of confirmation dialog");
</code></pre> <p>See Translations.</p>

Function Description <code>delete_doc(doctype, docname, callback)</code> Show a confirm dialog. On confirm, call <code>frappe.client.delete</code>, remove the document from <code>locals</code>, then call <code>callback(r, rt)</code>. <code>rename_doc(doctype, docname, callback)</code> Open the rename dialog. On confirm, call <code>frappe.rename_doc</code> with the new name and the merge flag. Updates <code>locals</code> and triggers the <code>rename</code> event on <code>document</code>. Calls <code>callback(new_name)</code>. <code>open_mapped_doc(opts)</code> Call <code>frappe.model.mapper.make_mapped_doc</code> (<code>POST</code>) and open the new document. See the options below. <code>add_mapped_doc_guard(fn)</code> Add <code>fn(mapped_doc, opts)</code>. If it returns <code>false</code> (or a promise of <code>false</code>), <code>open_mapped_doc</code> does not open the new document. An error in a guard is logged and ignored. <code>remove_mapped_doc_guard(fn)</code> Remove a guard. <code>should_open_mapped_doc(mapped_doc, opts)</code> Run all guards. Returns a promise of <code>true</code> or <code>false</code>. <p>Options of <code>open_mapped_doc(opts)</code>:</p> Option Description <code>method</code> Dotted path of a whitelisted mapper method on the server. <code>frm</code> The source form. If the form has unsaved changes, the call throws. Its name is the default <code>source_name</code>. Its selected grid rows are sent as <code>selected_children</code>. <code>source_name</code> Name of the source document. <code>args</code> Extra arguments for the mapper method. <code>freeze_message</code> Message while the screen is frozen. <code>run_link_triggers</code> Run Link field triggers on the new document when it opens. <pre><code>// sample_app/sample_module/doctype/sample_order/sample_order.js
frappe.model.open_mapped_doc({
    method: "sample_app.sample_module.doctype.sample_order.sample_order.make_invoice",
    frm: cur_frm,
});
</code></pre>

Class (factory) Options Methods <code>frappe.ui.Combobox</code> (<code>frappe.ui.combobox(opts)</code> returns the trigger) <code>options</code> (rows <code>{ label, value, description, icon, image, avatar, badge, disabled }</code>, groups, or a function <code>(query, { start })</code>), <code>page_size</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>placeholder</code>, <code>search_placeholder</code>, <code>filterable</code> (<code>true</code>), <code>hide_search</code>, <code>clear_button</code> (<code>true</code>), <code>tab_selects</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code>filters</code>, <code>footer</code>, <code>chevron</code>, <code>value_input</code>, <code>open_on_focus</code>, <code>arrow_keys_open</code>, <code>actions</code>, <code>before_open</code>, <code>on_change(value, option)</code>, <code>on_open</code>, <code>on_close(reason)</code> <code>get_value()</code>, <code>set_value(value, { label, image, avatar, silent = true })</code>, <code>clear()</code>, <code>set_options(options)</code>, <code>set_disabled(disabled)</code>, <code>focus()</code>, <code>open({ motion, query })</code>, <code>close(reason)</code> <code>frappe.ui.MultiCombobox</code> (<code>frappe.ui.multi_combobox(opts)</code>) Combobox options, plus <code>value</code> (list), <code>one_line</code>, <code>pill_href(value)</code>, <code>on_change(values, option, { added })</code> <code>get_value()</code> (list), <code>set_value(values)</code>, <code>add_value(entry)</code>, <code>remove_value(value)</code>, <code>clear()</code> <code>frappe.ui.Tabs</code> (<code>frappe.ui.tabs(opts)</code> returns the root, instance on <code>.data("es-tabs")</code>) <code>tabs</code> (<code>{ label, icon, content, disabled }</code>), <code>active</code> (0), <code>vertical</code>, <code>on_change(index, tab)</code> <code>set_active(index, { silent })</code>, <code>get_active()</code>, <code>destroy()</code> <code>frappe.ui.TabButtons</code> (<code>frappe.ui.tab_buttons(opts)</code>, instance on <code>.data("es-tab-buttons")</code>) <code>options</code> (<code>{ label, value, icon, icon_left, icon_right, active, disabled, title, onclick, prefix, suffix }</code>), <code>label</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>type</code> (<code>subtle</code>, <code>ghost</code>, <code>underline</code>, <code>browser-tab</code>), <code>size</code>, <code>vertical</code>, <code>direction</code>, <code>on_change(value, option)</code> <code>get_value()</code>, <code>set_value(value, { silent })</code> <code>frappe.ui.Progress</code> (<code>frappe.ui.progress(opts)</code>, <code>.html(opts)</code>, instance on <code>.data("es-progress")</code>) <code>value</code> (0 to 100), <code>size</code> (<code>sm</code> to <code>xl</code>), <code>label</code>, <code>hint</code> (<code>true</code> or a function), <code>intervals</code>, <code>interval_count</code> (6) <code>set_value(value)</code>, <code>get_value()</code>, <code>set_label(label)</code> <code>frappe.ui.Stepper</code> (<code>frappe.ui.stepper(opts)</code> returns <code>$el</code>) <code>steps</code> (<code>{ label, content }</code>), <code>current</code> (0), <code>label</code>, <code>is_locked(i)</code>, <code>is_completed(i)</code>, <code>on_step_click(i)</code>, <code>on_locked_click(i)</code>, <code>compact</code>, <code>hint</code>, <code>orientation</code>, <code>label_position</code> <code>set_current(index)</code>, <code>next_step()</code>, <code>prev_step()</code>, <code>refresh()</code> <pre><code>const $tabs = frappe.ui.tabs({
    tabs: [
        { label: __("Open"), content: () =&gt; $("&lt;div&gt;").text(__("Open orders"))[0] },
        { label: __("Closed"), content: __("No closed orders") },
    ],
