Name Bundle Description <code>frappe.ui.stat_card(opts)</code>, <code>frappe.ui.stat_cards({ items, layout = "grid" })</code> <code>desk_charts.bundle.js</code> Metric card: <code>label</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>delta</code> (<code>{ value, positive_is_good, suffix }</code>), <code>caption</code>, <code>dot</code>, <code>icon</code>, <code>loading</code>, <code>onclick</code>. <code>frappe.ui.OptionalSections</code> (<code>frappe.ui.optional_sections(opts)</code>) <code>optional_sections.bundle.js</code> Sections the user adds with a button: <code>sections</code> (<code>{ title, content, added }</code>), <code>label</code>, <code>remove_label</code>, <code>on_add</code>, <code>on_remove</code>. Methods <code>add(i)</code>, <code>remove(i)</code>, <code>is_added(i)</code>, <code>destroy()</code>. <code>frappe.ui.BottomSheet</code> (<code>frappe.ui.bottom_sheet(opts)</code>) <code>bottom_sheet.bundle.js</code> Phone sheet: <code>title</code>, <code>subtitle</code>, <code>header</code>, <code>content</code>, <code>options</code>, <code>footer</code>, <code>height</code> (<code>auto</code>, <code>half</code>, <code>full</code>), <code>snap_points</code>, <code>show_close</code>, <code>dismissible</code> (<code>true</code>), <code>on_open</code>, <code>on_close(reason)</code>. Methods <code>open()</code>, <code>close(reason)</code>, <code>toggle()</code>, <code>push(step)</code>, <code>pop()</code>, <code>set_title(title, subtitle)</code>, <code>set_options(options)</code>, <code>set_height(height)</code>, <code>destroy()</code>. <pre><code>await frappe.require("desk_charts.bundle.js");
frappe.ui.stat_card({ label: __("Open Orders"), value: "12", delta: { value: 8 } }).appendTo(page.main);
</code></pre>

Function Description <code>get_form_link(doctype, name, html = false, display_text = null, query_params_obj = null)</code> Desk URL of a form, for example <code>/desk/sample-item/Item%20A</code>. With <code>html</code>, an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag. <code>query_params_obj</code> adds a query string. <code>generate_route(item)</code> Desk URL of a workspace link item (<code>type</code>: <code>doctype</code>, <code>report</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>dashboard</code>, <code>workspace</code>, plus <code>doc_view</code>, <code>route_options</code>, <code>is_query_report</code> and others). <code>get_route_label(route_str)</code> Display label of a route string, for example <code>&lt;b&gt;ToDo&lt;/b&gt; List</code>. <code>get_url_arg(name)</code> Value of a query parameter of the current URL, or <code>""</code>. <code>get_query_string(url)</code> Part of <code>url</code> after <code>?</code>. <code>get_query_params(query_string)</code> Object of query parameters. Default: the current URL. Repeated keys give a list. <code>+</code> becomes a space. <code>make_query_string(obj, encode = true)</code> <code>?key=value&amp;...</code>. Skips <code>undefined</code>, <code>null</code> and <code>""</code>. Objects become JSON. <code>get_url_from_dict(args)</code> <code>key=value&amp;...</code> without <code>?</code>. Skips <code>null</code>. <code>get_args_dict_from_url(txt)</code> Object from <code>a=1&amp;b=2</code>. <code>sanitise_redirect(url)</code> <code>url</code> if it is on the same origin, else <code>""</code>. Keeps the relative or absolute form. <code>strip_url(url)</code> Remove characters before the protocol, <code>//</code> or <code>#</code>. <code>get_file_link(filename)</code> <code>files/&lt;filename&gt;</code> for a bare name. URLs and paths are returned as they are. <code>get_link_title(doctype, name)</code> Cached title of a Link value, or <code>undefined</code>. <code>add_link_title(doctype, name, value)</code> Add a title to the cache. <code>fetch_link_title(doctype, name)</code> Get the title from <code>frappe.desk.search.get_link_title</code> and cache it. Resolves with the title, or <code>name</code> on error. <code>get_page_view_count(route)</code> Call <code>frappe.website.doctype.web_page_view.web_page_view.get_page_view_count</code>. Returns the call. <pre><code>frappe.utils.get_form_link("Sample Item", "Item A", true, "Open");
// '&lt;a href="/desk/sample-item/Item%20A"&gt;Open&lt;/a&gt;'
frappe.utils.make_query_string({ a: 1, b: "x y", c: null }); // "?a=1&amp;b=x%20y"
frappe.utils.get_query_params("a=1&amp;b=x+y&amp;a=2");             // { a: ["1", "2"], b: "x y" }
</code></pre>

Function Description <code>get_mapped_doc(from_doctype, from_docname, table_maps, target_doc=None, postprocess=None, ignore_permissions=False, ignore_child_tables=False, cached=False)</code> Return a new unsaved document mapped from a source document. Checks <code>read</code> on the source and <code>create</code> on the target. Runs <code>before_mapping</code> and <code>after_mapping</code> on the target. <code>map_doc(source_doc, target_doc, table_map, source_parent=None)</code> Map one document with one table map. <code>map_fields(source_doc, target_doc, table_map, source_parent)</code> Copy fields with the same name, <code>field_map</code> fields and <code>fetch_from</code> values. <code>map_fetch_fields(target_doc, df, no_copy_fields)</code> Fill <code>fetch_from</code> fields of one Link field. <code>map_child_doc(source_d, target_parent, table_map, source_parent=None)</code> Map one child row and append it to the target. <code>make_mapped_doc(method: str, source_name: str, selected_children=None, args=None)</code> Call a whitelisted mapper method. <code>args</code> go to <code>frappe.flags.args</code>. Whitelisted. <code>map_docs(method: str, source_names: str \| list, target_doc, args=None)</code> Call a whitelisted mapper method once per source on one target. Whitelisted. <p><code>table_maps</code> is a dict keyed by source DocType. Keys of each map:</p> Key Description <code>doctype</code> Target DocType. Required. <code>field_map</code> Dict (or list of pairs) of source field to target field. <code>field_no_map</code> Fields not to copy. <code>validation</code> <code>{"field": ["=", value]}</code>. Throws if the source does not match. <code>postprocess</code> <code>fn(source, target, source_parent)</code> for this map. <code>condition</code> <code>fn(source_row)</code>. Rows where it returns falsy are skipped. <code>filter</code> <code>fn(source_row)</code>. Rows where it returns truthy are skipped. <code>ignore</code> Skip all rows of this child DocType. <code>add_if_empty</code> Map rows only if the target table is empty. <code>reset_value</code> Empty the target table first. <code>on_parent</code> Parent document (dict, JSON or document) when the target is a child row. <p>A child table with no map is copied when source and target have the same fieldname and child DocType and neither field is <code>no_copy</code>. Fields with <code>no_copy</code>, standard fields and table fields are not copied by name.</p> <pre><code>from frappe.model.mapper import get_mapped_doc

@frappe.whitelist()
def make_copy(source_name: str):
    return get_mapped_doc(
        "Sample Order",
        source_name,
        {
            "Sample Order": {"doctype": "Sample Order", "field_no_map": ["status"]},
